          "guid": "mt6mnbuvwfy7nkfj",
          "message": {
            "text": "Shrinking legacy radial gradients reverse both circles and the stop parameter. Blink and Skia accept either radius ordering, while SVG requires fr <= r; the paired reversal preserves the two-point conical function without fitting pixels or changing a tolerance. The 119-row source oracle and DPR browser suite cover this branch.",
            "markdown": "Shrinking legacy radial gradients reverse both circles and the stop parameter. Blink and Skia accept either radius ordering, while SVG requires fr <= r; the paired reversal preserves the two-point conical function without fitting pixels or changing a tolerance. The 119-row source oracle and DPR browser suite cover this branch."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/gradients.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 683,
                  "endLine": 701,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  if (gradient.legacyCircles != null) {\n    const geometry = computeLegacyRadialGeometry(gradient.legacyCircles, rect);\n    // SVG requires `fr <= r`, whereas Blink/Skia's two-point conical shader\n    // accepts either radius ordering. Reversing both circles and the stop\n    // parameter preserves the exact shader while satisfying SVG's grammar.\n    const shrinking = geometry.r1 > geometry.r2;\n    const stops = (shrinking\n      ? [...gradient.stops].reverse().map((stop) => ({ ...stop, offset: 1 - (stop.offset ?? 0) }))\n      : gradient.stops).map((stop) => stopMarkup(stop)).join(\"\");\n    const inner = shrinking\n      ? { x: geometry.x2, y: geometry.y2, r: geometry.r2 }\n      : { x: geometry.x1, y: geometry.y1, r: geometry.r1 };\n    const outer = shrinking\n      ? { x: geometry.x1, y: geometry.y1, r: geometry.r1 }\n      : { x: geometry.x2, y: geometry.y2, r: geometry.r2 };\n    return `<radialGradient id=\"${id}\" gradientUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" fx=\"${num(inner.x)}\" fy=\"${num(inner.y)}\" fr=\"${num(inner.r)}\" cx=\"${num(outer.x)}\" cy=\"${num(outer.y)}\" r=\"${num(outer.r)}\">${stops}</radialGradient>`;\n  }\n  const cx = resolvePos(gradient.position.x, rect.x, rect.w);\n  const cy = resolvePos(gradient.position.y, rect.y, rect.h);"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
